.UPDATE...
Issued at 945 AM PDT Fri Aug 14 2026

Overall, the short term forecast remains unchanged this morning.
24 hour temperature departures were running 5 to 7 degrees lower
thanks to plentiful cloud cover across a majority of the area.
Hourly temperatures through early afternoon were adjusted
downward to account for ongoing trends. Drizzle has persisted per
FAA and area web cams and a few more bucket tips are anticipated
along the immediate coastline through early this afternoon.
Gradual clearing is anticipated, but the timing should be similar
to what was observed yesterday based on the latest short term NWP
and trends (early to mid afternoon). MaxT remains unchanged and
I`m still anticipating today`s (Friday) highs in the 60s and 70s
with 80s across the valley locations along the US HWY 101
corridor. There`s some uncertainty across the North Bay with
respect to the clearing time as a pronounced eddy has developed
across Bodega Bay. This feature was present yesterday, however,
and areas did scatter out during the mid to late afternoon. This
seems plausible to repeat today. Onshore flow should translate to
winds accelerating through gaps and passes, with peak gusts
potentially as great as 40 mph in some of the wind corridors this
afternoon and into the pre-dawn hours on Saturday.

