.SHORT TERM...
Issued at 1101 PM PDT Thu Aug 13 2026
(Tonight through Saturday)

Upper-level shortwave troughing will bring the coolest conditions of
the week with well below normal temperatures and a deep marine layer
Friday. The 00Z sounding observed a marine layer of 2,400 feet with
satellite already showing an inland intrusion through the Delta and
Pacheco Pass. With the associated lift from the aforementioned
trough, drizzle can be expected along the coast and in the higher
terrain via orographic lift. Smoke from the Timber Fire is expected
to improve with the help of northwesterly transport winds.

&&

.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1101 PM PDT Thu Aug 13 2026
(Saturday night through next Thursday)

Gradual warming trend kicks off Saturday as upper-level ridging
builds into the Desert Southwest. Simultaneously, upper-level
troughing will develop well off the West Coast. This will keep the
ridge in check and onshore flow in place with temperatures remaining
below normal. The marine layer will likely be deeper in the Bay Area
than in the Central Coast with a chance for drizzle remaining across
the coast and higher terrain. Global ensemble clusters are in
agreement through Tuesday and then by Wednesday 60% show troughing
prevailing into Thursday. Sensible weather wise, this would result
in a cooling trend with increased onshore flow and the deepening of
the marine layer.

