.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 610 AM PDT Fri Aug 14 2026

The marine layer is around 2000-2500ft leaving the area with
widespread stratus and pockets of coastal drizzle. Cigs will take a
bit longer to clear this morning, generally by the late morning for
most sites. Breezy onshore winds return this afternoon and evening,
with another night of cloudy skies and MVFR cigs on tap. Medium to
high confidence in the forecast.

 Vicinity of SFO...Low clouds and reports of drizzle have come
across Bay Area terminals including, KSFO. Expect this to continue
through the next couple of hours, with conditions improving by mid
to late morning. The question for SFO today is whether or not the
site clears. Some models keep stratus on the western half of the TAF
ring which could leave us with SCT to BKN MVFR cigs through the
afternoon. Kept a slightly more optimistic forecast with more of the
FEW and SCT clouds, with stratus returning near or after sunset.
Medium confidence in the forecast.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...The marine layer is around 2000-2500ft
leaving the area with widespread stratus and pockets of coastal
drizzle. Cigs will take a bit longer to clear this morning, but may
struggle to actually clear at all today for KMRY.Stratus returns
early, and will likely fall to MVFR between 01-03Z. Medium
confidence in the forecast.

