.MARINE...
(Today through Wednesday)
Issued at 933 AM PDT Fri Aug 14 2026

Gentle to moderate northwest winds will continue through early
next week. Seas will continue to subside and become moderate in
response. A long period southerly swell of about 16 to 18 seconds
approaches the coast tonight into Sunday. Winds will freshen
early to mid next week, causing seas to build up to 9 feet. Light
drizzle is possible across the coastal waters. Haze and smoke may
also impact visibility along the Big Sur coastline due to the
Timber fire.

